WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:05.050
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan, and
in this video I'm breaking down the ending

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:08.460
of Cobra Kai Season 3, what it means for Season
4,

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.920
and revealing all the clever details and secret
easter eggs to previous seasons and all the

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.340
Karate Kid movies.

00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:17.010
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:21.119
After several seasons of "will they, won't
they?", Daniel and Johnny have finally joined

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:26.099
karate forces to solve their shared problem:
how to give Kreese and his Cobra Kai the chop

00:00:26.099 --> 00:00:27.179
for good.

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:31.170
Teaching Kreese a lesson wasn't really something
Daniel thought he was up to before, as he

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:34.410
told us back in the 80s:
"That guy just doesn't know what karate's

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:35.410
all about."

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:36.460
"Yeah, well, maybe he should learn."

00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:39.070
"Would you like to teach him?"

00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:40.070
"No."

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.359
I wouldn't be surprised if we see that moment
mentioned in some way in Season 4;

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:48.179
after all, the showrunners are self-professed
super-fans that go deep with their references

00:00:48.179 --> 00:00:52.910
from visual nods like Fernandez Meats stickers
to episode titles like Ace Degenerate.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:55.340
"You're still the Ace degenerate."

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:56.340
"No, ex-degenerate, man."

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.809
Indeed, Johnny's come quite a way even just
this season.

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:03.030
I mean, look how in episode one he's punching
car windows à la John Kreese;

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:07.010
but, by the end, he couldn't be further removed
from his old sensei as he's teamed up with

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:08.320
his old rival.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.870
As Mr Miyagi put it in one of his letters
that Kumiko reads to Danny,

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.720
"In life, we'll always lose our way.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:19.650
But it is people, not the signs, that guide
us back to the right path."

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.570
Now, the season finale saw friends who'd become
enemies reunited as friends once more.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.620
And while Daniel and Johnny might not be best
buds exactly,

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:31.730
"Have the man-boys filled you in on the whole
'mortal enemy karate dojo battle for the soul

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.030
of the Valley' thing?"

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.660
they are allies now at least, so they're on
the right path.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:39.390
After all, as Ali told them:
"And the truth is..

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.390
you guys are more alike than you want to admit."

00:01:41.390 --> 00:01:44.760
Or as Kreese would say:
"The enemy of your enemy...

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.260
is your friend."

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:50.030
Interestingly, when Kreese said those words
to Hawk earlier this season, he was talking

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:54.780
about Robby, who'd put their fellow Cobra
Miguel in a coma but had now turned against

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.130
Daniel and Miyagi-Do.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:01.130
So, it's clear that Kreese is just using Robby
to get what he wants: revenge.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:04.950
"You know, when I was overseas, it was hard
to tell who was the enemy."

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:09.770
In fact, Kreese has got Robby so brainwashed,
thinking that mercy is a weakness for losers,

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:13.980
that he can't see Kreese is the real enemy,
not his dad or Daniel.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:15.300
"I won't fight you."

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:16.300
"You are weak."

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.730
Indeed, Robby thinks Kreese is the good guy:
"He only wants what's best for you."

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:24.370
Given everything Johnny knows about his old
sensei, seeing his kid side with him and the

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:27.590
way Kreese calls Robby 'son' must really hurt.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:32.400
After all, we saw how Johnny reacted when
he discovered Daniel was training Robby in

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.420
Season 1.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:37.660
Still, as Daniel told Johnny this season:
"The whole reason these kids got into trouble

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:41.220
was because of us;
we can't let them suffer because of our issues;

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:43.370
the only way to end this is by working together."

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:48.300
In other words, just as Kreese told Daniel
in episode 1 about their eventual face-off,

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.040
this was all inevitable.

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:54.530
And that's because this whole situation is
as much about the past as it is the present.

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:55.745
And the title of the finale, December 19,
confirms that.

00:02:55.745 --> 00:02:59.220
The showrunners have said they really care
about their titles, and often tie them thematically

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.040
to the episode's content and to the original
movies.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:06.940
And the date in this title does both, as it's
the day Daniel beat Johnny in the 1984 All

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.430
Valley Tournament.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:12.560
Kreese still hasn't got over what happened
that day as his whole philosophy of life and

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:16.300
karate lost to Mr Miyagi's diametrically opposed
ethos.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.570
Although his own actions afterwards caused
him to lose all his students and go broke,

00:03:21.570 --> 00:03:23.850
he placed the blame elsewhere.

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:28.300
And while his and his old army buddy's schemes
for payback at the next tournament failed

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:31.940
in the Karate Kid 3, he's obviously hoping
it's third time lucky:

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:34.350
"Why don't we settle this the old-fashioned
way?

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:35.350
Tournament.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.350
If we lose...

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.350
I go.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.350
If you lose..."

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.350
"We won't lose."

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:43.010
But will Kreese actually leave peacefully
if he does lose?

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:46.260
Quite possibly not, because as Johnny said,
"You can't trust him!"

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:51.180
By the way, notice how Kreese looks at Johnny
when he says "if you lose" because he's goading

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:56.250
him about his second place back in '84, something
Kreese took personally:

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.520
"Second place is no place!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:58.520
You're off the team!

00:03:58.520 --> 00:03:59.520
You're nothing!

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.520
You lost.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.520
You're a loser!"

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.739
This season went into Kreese's backstory,
and we learned that as a young man he was

00:04:04.739 --> 00:04:10.631
more like Hawk, Miguel, or Tory, dealing with
a rough life, family hardships, and bullies.

00:04:10.631 --> 00:04:14.940
And, like them, he took to heart some flawed
lessons from an authority figure, modelling

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:19.389
himself after his Captain in Vietnam,
adopting not just his interest in martial

00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:24.949
arts and his cigar habit, but most damagingly,
his 'kill or be killed', 'shed your humanity',

00:04:24.949 --> 00:04:26.749
merciless attitude.

00:04:26.749 --> 00:04:29.610
Kreese led his students down that same wrong
path;

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:34.219
and decades later, one of them did the same
with his own students, until he wised up.

00:04:34.219 --> 00:04:39.479
But with Kreese in the Cobra Kai driving seat
again, he's perpetuating the cruel 'no mercy'

00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:43.210
cycle, passing it on to a new generation,
This will never be over LaRusso.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:50.180
You hear me?"
and treating schoolkids like they're in a

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.050
war:
Fighting his mentor in Vietnam was a seminal

00:04:53.050 --> 00:04:55.710
moment for Kreese becoming the man we know
today.

00:04:55.710 --> 00:05:00.520
Interestingly, it only happened because he
stepped in to save his army pal, Silver.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:04.539
But when their allies arrived bringing with
them the possibility that both Kreese and

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:08.699
his Captain could make it out of their battle
to the death alive, Kreese made a choice about

00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:10.550
the kind of man he wanted to be.

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:15.789
In a way, in the finale, Johnny is also only
there fighting his mentor because of someone

00:05:15.789 --> 00:05:18.509
else;
his protégé, Miguel, who's been badly beaten

00:05:18.509 --> 00:05:20.629
by the Cobra Kai kids.

00:05:20.629 --> 00:05:25.419
And just as Kreese took over from his Captain
after their fight, season 4 will likely bring

00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:27.800
a similar opportunity for Johnny.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:32.650
But back in the here and now, Johnny refuses
to fight his son as, unlike Kreese, he's no

00:05:32.650 --> 00:05:37.639
longer willing to continue his mentor's merciless
cycle with the younger generation, because

00:05:37.639 --> 00:05:41.009
as he told his students:
"I wasn't taught the difference between mercy

00:05:41.009 --> 00:05:43.100
and honor and I paid the price for it."

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.800
In fact, he even vetoed them fighting dirty.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.840
"The baddest badass is the one who beats his
opponent when he's at his strongest.

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:51.330
Not when his back is turned."

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:56.180
But just as Kreese's Captain tried to exploit
his humanity by revealing his girlfriend's

00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:01.129
death right before their fight, Kreese himself
is happy to take advantage of Johnny's humanity

00:06:01.129 --> 00:06:03.380
as he tends to his unconscious son.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:08.449
And look what's in shot right after that:
an All Valley tournament poster, reminding

00:06:08.449 --> 00:06:11.659
us what this is all about and how it will
end.

00:06:11.659 --> 00:06:16.479
Kreese reverts to his old Karate Kid Part
II ways when he starts to choke Johnny.

00:06:16.479 --> 00:06:20.419
It's not the first time we've seen Kreese
get him in a chokehold in this series, though

00:06:20.419 --> 00:06:24.880
last time he was demonstrating the move in
class, rather than actually trying to take

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.880
him out.

00:06:25.880 --> 00:06:29.770
But as Kreese said at the top of the season,
he thought he and Johnny would be fighting

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:33.210
Daniel together, which is what I think it
means when he tells Johnny:

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:35.550
"This isn't how I wanted this to end."

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:39.719
And the way he kicks his former student away
here after choking him reminds me of how Johnny

00:06:39.719 --> 00:06:44.740
pushed Kreese away after using the chokehold
on him when he first arrived back in season

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:45.740
2.

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:50.039
As for how Kreese deals with Daniel when he
turns up, let's just say there's definitely

00:06:50.039 --> 00:06:54.270
a recurring theme of smashing his opponents
into glass in the show.

00:06:54.270 --> 00:06:58.529
Which is likely a call-back to when he and
his buddy Silver fought Mr Miyagi in the third

00:06:58.529 --> 00:07:00.389
Karate Kid movie.

00:07:00.389 --> 00:07:05.520
Of course, in the second movie, Kreese also
kept smashing his fists into car windows as

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.630
he failed repeatedly to punch Danny's sensei.

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.710
And while Kreese can't stop resorting to dirty
tactics,

00:07:11.710 --> 00:07:17.229
"Time for you and Miyagi to reunite!"
he's once again outmanoeuvred by Miyagi-do

00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:21.020
techniques, this time the secret "pressure
points" that Chozen taught Danny.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:26.639
"If an enemy insists on war...
then you take away their ability to wage it."

00:07:26.639 --> 00:07:30.340
Given he was interrupted by his daughter,
I wonder if next season they'll address how

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.669
Danny would have ended the fight.

00:07:32.669 --> 00:07:36.319
It certainly didn't feel like he was going
out in Mr Miyagi style.

00:07:36.319 --> 00:07:40.949
A couple of other interesting details here
are the colours Daniel and Johnny are wearing,

00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:44.069
reminiscent of their showdown at the end of
the film.

00:07:44.069 --> 00:07:49.099
Also, this image of Sam with her father and
Miguel beside Johnny just as Robby arrives

00:07:49.099 --> 00:07:53.349
would doubtless reinforce in Robby's mind
his earlier accusation that his dad treats

00:07:53.349 --> 00:07:56.169
Miguel more like a son than him.

00:07:56.169 --> 00:08:00.639
And just as the season 2 finale used a phone
to foreshadow the return of another original

00:08:00.639 --> 00:08:05.059
movie character for the next season,
this time a phone call by Kreese lets us know

00:08:05.059 --> 00:08:09.551
that the third film's main villain, his army
pal Terry Silver, will be turning up in Season

00:08:09.551 --> 00:08:10.551
4.

00:08:10.551 --> 00:08:15.699
In the show, a young Silver goes by the nickname
Twig and only makes it out of Vietnam alive

00:08:15.699 --> 00:08:16.780
thanks to his friend.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:17.929
"I owe you, man.

00:08:17.929 --> 00:08:19.090
You saved my ass.

00:08:19.090 --> 00:08:20.090
Anything you need...

00:08:20.090 --> 00:08:21.090
I'm there for you.

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:22.090
You hear me, Johnny?

00:08:22.090 --> 00:08:23.090
Your whole life!

00:08:23.090 --> 00:08:24.090
I owe you."

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:27.399
Given the phone call then, it looks like we'll
see actor Thomas Ian Griffith, who played

00:08:27.399 --> 00:08:31.559
Silver in the movie, back in action;
especially as he said only last year that

00:08:31.559 --> 00:08:33.880
"it would be fun to see the whole gang" again.

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:38.940
Silver's been happily repaying Kreese's life-saving
over the years, from founding Cobra Kai for

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:43.440
him to wreaking revenge on Daniel and Miyagi
when Kreese went out of business.

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:48.600
And with just how much Silver revelled in
sneaking around and inflicting pain and humiliation

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:51.880
back in the 80s,
I'm sure he'll love teaming up with Kreese

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:56.740
again to give Daniel, Johnny, and their students
a taste of the nasty medicine he thinks they

00:08:56.740 --> 00:08:59.760
deserve for everything they've done to his
old army friend.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.920
I wonder what devious schemes he'll dream
up this time!

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:08.170
Now, when it came to fighting Silver and Kreese
in the movie, Mr Miyagi easily defeated them,

00:09:08.170 --> 00:09:10.560
but how will Daniel and Johnny do in the show?

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:15.310
Of course, Ralph Macchio and William Zabka
are the stars of the series, so they'll certainly

00:09:15.310 --> 00:09:20.300
triumph in the end, but the writers have got
ten episodes, that's over five hours, compared

00:09:20.300 --> 00:09:21.310
to a two-hour movie.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:26.089
So, I imagine we'll get some stand-offs between
the adult leads before their final big showdown,

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:31.339
and a lot of training and confrontations for
the younger characters before the tournament!

00:09:31.339 --> 00:09:35.350
And if you haven't had enough Cobra Kai yet,
you can discover more of the amazing details

00:09:35.350 --> 00:09:38.440
cleverly hidden in the show in my Things You
Missed video.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:41.520
Tap here to watch that or follow the link
in the video description.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:44.220
So, what did you think of the latest season?

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:46.380
And what would you like to see happen in season
4?

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:48.380
Leave your comments below!

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:52.690
And if you enjoyed this, don't forget to leave
a thumbs-up, it's hugely appreciated.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:56.980
Now tap left for my next video or tap right
for something else you're sure to like.

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.889
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

00:09:58.889 --> 00:09:59.870
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

